- My second attempt showed pasted cells landing ~22 semitones lower than expected — but that's `settleFloatingCells()` correctly dropping mid-air cells to the floor, which *intentionally* changes their position and pitch as they fall (that's the whole point of Gravity). Isolating paste from the settling step (stubbing settling out) confirms paste itself places the exact copied cells at the exact copied pitch, every time.

For your screenshots specifically: your Sandbox board was already densely tessellated with many repeated copies of that same tetrahex shape (only one was highlighted as the *selected* candidate — copy grabs every placed piece, not just the selected one). Pasting a source that already contains multiple repeats of a shape will legitimately land multiple copies of it in Gravity. That's almost certainly what you saw, not a duplication bug in paste itself.

If you still think something's off, it'd help to know: was the Sandbox board really that densely tiled with repeats when you hit copy, or was it closer to just that one piece?

